from pathlib import Path

root=Path('client-testimonials')
projects=[
('limitlessbrainlab','Limitless Brain Lab','https://www.limitlessbrainlab.com/','Brain-health service combining qEEG/NeuroSense360 assessments, cognitive care, counselling and home/clinic programmes.','The site presents Protect My Brain and Treat My Brain paths, a Measure–Monitor–Manage model, home assessments, clinic support, and a named founder, Dr. Sweta Adatia. Public page claims include 50K+ customers, 5K+ brain maps and 442 Google reviews; these are site claims, not project outcomes.','qEEG assessment journey; clear distinction between preventive and treatment paths; trust and clinical-claim substantiation should be checked.', 'medical/health founder or programme lead','education and trust in a sensitive healthcare journey'),
('enerex','Enerex','https://enerex.com/','Energy-operations platform for brokers and suppliers, covering CRM, pricing, contracts, commissions, compliance, data and partner discovery.','The site is organised around BrokerHub, SupplierHub, DataHub and MarketHub, with demo CTAs and role-based navigation. It publishes a customer quote from Michael Harris of Unified Energy and several company-reported scale claims.','information architecture for multiple audiences; demo conversion; product proof and large numerical claims need validation; page copy is dense in places.', 'B2B marketing lead or product marketer','making a complex platform easier to understand'),
('balletpro','BalletPro','https://www.balletpro.co.uk/','UK dance retail shop specialising in pointe accessories, dancewear, exercise equipment, foot health and related products.','Shopify storefront with collection-led navigation, product reviews, stockist search, trade enquiry and a prominent set of customer quotes. The page names Amanda and team in one quote but does not establish a project relationship with Abdul.','product discovery across specialist categories; mobile filtering/search; delivery and advice messaging; stock and review states should be tested.', 'e-commerce manager or founder','reducing friction in a specialist retail journey'),
('cuddlespetbrand','Cuddles Dog Bakery','https://cuddlespetbrand.com/','Baytown, Texas home-based pet bakery selling handmade dog treats, cakes, pupcakes, gift items and local services.','Shopify storefront emphasises handmade, all-natural, small-batch treats, local pickup, wholesale and a pupcake bar. Collections separate everyday treats from local birthday cakes.','local-pickup clarity; product options and sold-out states; distinguishing shipping products from local-only cakes; social proof could be strengthened if real reviews exist.', 'founder or small-business e-commerce lead','making a warm local brand easier to shop'),
('myzochocolate','MYZO Chocolate','https://myzochocolate.com/','Direct-to-consumer bean-to-bar chocolate brand built around single-origin Costa Rican cacao, with bars, bundles and subscriptions.','Shopify site positions the product as Costa Rican cacao, crafted in Ukraine and envisioned in Miami. It offers single bars, gift boxes and a three-bar subscription; product pages display review counts.','storytelling across origin, making and purchase; collection/product consistency; sold-out states and seasonal shipping notice; review provenance should be confirmed.', 'founder or brand/e-commerce manager','turning product story into a clearer buying path'),
('bidet-toilets','Bidet Toilets Store','https://bidet-toilets.co.uk/','UK e-commerce retailer for bidet toilets, smart toilets, seats, frames and concealed cisterns from brands including Geberit, TOTO, VitrA and Grohe.','The storefront offers wall-hung, close-coupled and floor-standing paths, brand navigation, product comparison, UK support, two-year guarantee and 30-day returns messaging.','high-consideration product comparison; installation/support information; trust signals and shipping/returns wording; duplicated promotional blocks should be reviewed.', 'e-commerce manager or technical product lead','helping shoppers compare a complex product category'),
('farawayfinds','Faraway Finds','https://farawayfinds.co.uk/','UK online retail brand; the homepage exposes international country/currency selection and free UK shipping messaging.','Publicly crawlable content is dominated by a large country/region selector and store chrome, so the catalogue and proposition need a fuller client-approved review before specific claims are made.','internationalisation and first-load clarity; country selector accessibility; navigation and product proposition are confirmation items.', 'founder or e-commerce manager','finding and prioritising storefront issues where evidence is limited'),
('mrca','Manufacturing Revitalization Corporation of America','https://mrca.net/','Investment and operating group focused on revitalising legacy US manufacturing companies and supporting employee ownership, modernization and continuity.','The site explains its mission, portfolio companies, manufacturing focus, employee-ownership plan and a large visual/video-led presentation. It links to portfolio companies including Wells Industries and others.','enterprise narrative and portfolio architecture; accessible handling of video/image-led content; clear separation of corporate facts from future plans.', 'corporate marketing lead or communications manager','making a complex portfolio story easier to follow'),
('wellsind','Wells Industries','https://wellsind.com/','El Paso manufacturer of custom hospitality furniture, using metal, wood, stone and other materials for hotels, restaurants and public spaces.','Shopify site presents custom furniture, local production, a 70,000-square-foot facility, nearly 80 team members, capabilities, gallery and case-study-style work for hotel brands.','specification-led discovery; project/capability hierarchy; gallery performance and alt text; enquiry path and case-study evidence should be tested.', 'marketing manager or sales lead','connecting visual proof to a B2B enquiry journey'),
('wisconic','Wisconic','https://wisconic.com/','Midwestern US custom plastic injection molder offering molding, tooling, tool-mold design, distribution and private labeling.','Webflow site says it has operated since 1994, highlights American manufacturing, galleries, capabilities, industries served and links to an MRCA company video. It also presents automation, logistics and sustainability positioning.','capability navigation; balancing gallery content with enquiry CTAs; motion/video accessibility; claims about shipping, returns, automation and materials need evidence.', 'marketing lead or technical sales representative','clarifying a technical manufacturing offer without losing visual impact'),
]

angles=[
('Personal experience','A candid account of working with Abdul: what was unclear at first, how issues were explained, and what the client could see more clearly afterward.','seated, direct-to-camera','desk/work materials, annotated page, call notes, before/after issue list','calm, reflective','The useful part was having the problems explained clearly, not just pointed out.'),
('Specific project improvement','A focused QA/UX review of one evidence-based journey. Keep results descriptive; insert only confirmed fixes or measurements.','standing or interview-style, off-camera interviewer','screen recording, mobile test, product/category page, issue reproduction','precise, conversational','We could finally see where the experience needed attention.'),
('Team perspective','How a documented review could support prioritisation, handoff and re-testing. This is a draft perspective and must be spoken only by a real participant.','walking through workspace with occasional cutaways','ticket or checklist, team discussion, responsive layouts, retest notes','practical, lightly upbeat','It gave the team a shared list of things to resolve.'),
]

def script(p, n):
 slug,name,url,what,obs,imps,profile,theme=p
 angle,description,setting,broll,tone,key=angles[n]
 focus=imps.split(';')[0]
 openings=[
 f"Before this review, we knew the {theme} mattered, but we didn't have a very clear way to talk about the gaps.",
 f"One thing that stood out to me was how quickly the review moved from general impressions to a real customer journey on {name}.",
 f"For our team, the value wasn't a big headline number. It was having someone look at the site with fresh eyes and give us something we could work from."
 ]
 return f'''# Testimonial {n+1} — Suggested {profile}\n\n**Perspective:** {angle}. This is a first-person draft for a real client to correct, personalise and approve.\n\n**Approximate duration:** 60–75 seconds  \n**Tone:** {tone}  \n**Location / framing:** {setting}.  \n**Delivery:** Natural pace; pause after the first sentence and keep technical terms in the speaker's own words.  \n**B-roll:** {broll}.  \n**Seated / standing / walking:** {setting.split(',')[0]}.\n\n## Script\n\n> {openings[n]}\n>\n> Abdul Rehman's review helped us look at the site as a real person would use it. For {name}, that meant paying attention to {focus.lower()}. The useful thing was the way he separated what he could actually observe from what still needed checking. He didn't present a guess as a result, and he didn't promise a sales lift that we hadn't measured.\n>\n> He walked through the relevant pages, recorded the points that could cause confusion, and explained why each one mattered. **{key}** That made the conversation much easier for our team because we had specific examples rather than a long list of vague recommendations.\n>\n> The next step is to confirm which fixes were completed and what changed after re-testing. But even before that, the work gave us a clearer view of {theme}. I would describe it as a practical review that helped us decide what to investigate and improve next.\n\n**Key sentence to emphasise:** “{key}”\n'''

def claims(p):
 slug,name,url,what,obs,imps,profile,theme=p
 return f'''# Claims to Verify — {name}\n\nNo testimonial in this folder should be published as a client statement until a real speaker confirms the wording.\n\n## Confirm before recording\n- The identity, name, title and company of the speaker.\n- Whether Abdul Rehman worked on this website, and the exact scope: audit, QA, UX, technical review, issue reporting, prioritisation or re-testing.\n- Which observations were actually found during the project, on which pages/devices, and which fixes were made.\n- Any claim about improved speed, conversion, revenue, sales, traffic, rankings, accessibility compliance or reduced support requests.\n- Whether the site facts used in the draft are still current: {obs}\n- Any numerical or customer proof displayed on the public site. Treat it as a company-published claim, not as a result of Abdul's work.\n\n## Safe publishing note\nThe scripts are **drafts, not fabricated testimonials**. Replace generic passages with the client's own words and remove anything they cannot personally verify.\n'''

for p in projects:
 d=root/p[0]; d.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)
 slug,name,url,what,obs,imps,profile,theme=p
 (d/'research.md').write_text(f'''# Research Summary — {name}\n\n- **Company:** {name}\n- **Website:** {url}\n- **What they do:** {what}\n- **Research source:** Public homepage reviewed on 2026-10-03.\n\n## Verified public facts\n{obs}\n\n## Reasonable observations\n{imps}\n\n## Abdul Rehman's verified contribution\nNo project-specific contribution was supplied or independently verified in the source material available for this draft. The testimonials therefore use conditional language and must be corrected by the client before publication.\n\n## Information requiring confirmation\nSee [`claims-to-verify.md`](claims-to-verify.md).\n''')
 for i in range(3): (d/f'testimonial-0{i+1}.md').write_text(script(p,i))
 (d/'claims-to-verify.md').write_text(claims(p))

index=['# Client Testimonials and Review — Index\n','These are research-led, approval-ready drafts. **Status for every project: Draft — client confirmation required.**\n']
for p in projects: index.append(f'- [{p[1]}]({p[0]}/): 3 draft video concepts; claims pending confirmation.')
(root/'TESTIMONIAL-INDEX.md').write_text('\n'.join(index))
(root/'README.md').write_text('''# Client Testimonials and Review\n\nA separate, Git-ready set of testimonial research and video-script drafts for ten client websites. The material is designed to help a real client review, correct, personalise and approve a recording. It is not a collection of invented endorsements.\n\n## Methodology\n\nPublic homepages were reviewed individually on 2026-10-03. Company descriptions and visible product/service facts are recorded in each `research.md`. Reasonable UX observations are kept separate from verified facts. No sales, revenue, conversion, speed, ranking or traffic improvement is claimed without supplied evidence.\n\n## Sprint structure\n\n- Sprint 1: Limitless Brain Lab, Enerex, BalletPro\n- Sprint 2: Cuddles Dog Bakery, MYZO Chocolate, Bidet Toilets Store\n- Sprint 3: Faraway Finds, MRCA\n- Sprint 4: Wells Industries, Wisconic\n\n## Status\n\nAll 30 scripts are **draft — client confirmation required**. Speaker profiles are suggestions only. No name, title or company has been assigned to an unverified speaker.\n\n## Folder contents\n\nEach project folder contains `research.md`, three distinct `testimonial-0N.md` scripts and `claims-to-verify.md`. Use [`TESTIMONIAL-INDEX.md`](TESTIMONIAL-INDEX.md) to navigate all projects.\n\n## Verification requirements\n\n1. Confirm that Abdul Rehman worked on the project and define his actual contribution.\n2. Ask the real client to rewrite any sentence that does not sound like them.\n3. Confirm every issue, fix and project detail against tickets, recordings or acceptance notes.\n4. Add only measured KPI results with a dated source and permission to publish.\n5. Confirm speaker name, title, company, release consent and usage rights.\n6. Remove placeholders and any claim the speaker cannot personally stand behind.\n\n## Publishing checklist\n\n- [ ] Client approved the final words and approved the project description.\n- [ ] Speaker identity and release are documented.\n- [ ] Claims have evidence or have been softened to observations.\n- [ ] Medical, product, shipping, guarantee and performance claims are checked with the relevant owner.\n- [ ] Captions, transcript, audio, contrast, readable cutaways and B-roll permissions are complete.\n- [ ] Final video has a project label and no unsupported before/after implication.\n''')
print('created',len(projects),'projects')
